\section{Replay Edge Moves with Distinct Symbolic Values}

Backward obligations are useful over whole functions, but one can
check a parallel-copy resolver in isolation by forward replay. Assume
full-width mutually disjoint locations, a known incoming map at the
edge, and a sequence consisting only of legal same-width moves.
The edge contract specifies a source in the original map for every
required successor location, including any location deliberately left
unchanged. Distinct source locations can be assigned distinct symbols
for this test. That makes the check conservative if the allocator
would otherwise justify some of them by an equality not supplied here.

\begin{sudocode}[Validate a claimed edge transfer]
\State $before\gets$ fresh symbols for all defined incoming locations
\State $now\gets$ copy of $before$
\ForAll{moves $d\gets s$ in emitted order}
  \If{move is illegal or $s$ has no defined symbol in $now$}
    \State \Return failed at this move \Comment{Scratch starts undefined}
  \EndIf
  \State $now[d]\gets now[s]$
\EndFor
\ForAll{required pairs $(dest,source)$ in edge contract}
  \If{either endpoint is undefined in its corresponding map}
    \State \Return missing location
  \EndIf
  \If{$now[dest]\ne before[source]$}
    \State \Return failed at $dest$ \Comment{Compare to original source}
  \EndIf
\EndFor
\State \Return accepted
\end{sudocode}

With input $r_0=4,r_1=7,r_2=11$, let the successor require
$(r_0,r_1,r_2)=(7,11,4)$. Moves $s\gets r_0$, $r_0\gets r_1$,
$r_1\gets r_2$, $r_2\gets s$ pass. If $r_2$ instead reads $r_0$
at the last step, the actual tuple becomes $(7,11,7)$ and the
check names $r_2$. Add an identity requirement for $r_3=19$; a
mutant using $r_3$ for scratch without restoring it must now fail
even if the rotation itself works.

After every replayed move the symbolic map denotes exactly the copies
the machine would hold for every concrete input assignment. With
direct-indexed locations, cost is linear in locations, emitted moves
and obligations. The check is per edge; it says nothing about edge
placement or the incoming map's truth. Check those separately and
extend the replay to hardware units or byte ranges before admitting
partial writes. In a whole-function validator, attach the first
failure to the predecessor and successor IDs so that two edges into
the same join cannot be mistaken for one another.
